From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps4-gladius <ps4-gladius@invalid>
Date: Tue, 7 Oct 2026 19:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] server: report a fatal error through klog as well.

fatal_error writes to stderr and exits. On this console stderr goes nowhere, so
every message it has produced was discarded -- including the ones saying why
the server would not start. Worse, on PS4 the write itself took the title down
with an uncatchable SIGSYS, so a diagnosable failure became a bare address.

Finding the first of these messages meant symbolising klog's backtrace against
the module bases and then reading the format string out of the binary by
following the leaq operand. That is not a repeatable way to read an error.

sceKernelDebugOutText needs no descriptor, no configuration and no network, and
is synchronous -- which matters because the next statement is exit(). Send the
message there too, keeping the stderr write for every other platform.
---
diff --git a/server/request.c b/server/request.c
--- a/server/request.c
+++ b/server/request.c
@@ -149,12 +149,33 @@ void fatal_protocol_error( struct thread *thread, const char *err, ... )
     kill_thread( thread, 1 );
 }
 
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+extern int sceKernelDebugOutText( int channel, const char *text );
+#endif
+
 /* die on a fatal error */
 void fatal_error( const char *err, ... )
 {
     va_list args;
 
     va_start( args, err );
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    /* stderr goes nowhere on this console, so every message this function has
+     * ever produced was discarded -- including the ones explaining why the
+     * server would not start. sceKernelDebugOutText needs no descriptor, no
+     * configuration and no network, and is synchronous, which matters because
+     * the next statement is exit(). */
+    {
+        char line[512];
+        int n = snprintf( line, sizeof(line), "wineserver: " );
+        if (n < 0) n = 0;
+        if ((size_t)n < sizeof(line))
+            vsnprintf( line + n, sizeof(line) - (size_t)n, err, args );
+        sceKernelDebugOutText( 0, line );
+    }
+    va_end( args );
+    va_start( args, err );
+#endif
     fprintf( stderr, "wineserver: " );
     vfprintf( stderr, err, args );
     va_end( args );
-- 
